{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#152","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#152","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#152\",\"parent_revision\":\"1335fa854c41be9c6811e5791829faade73ece84e33e655b4e3e612cbfec641e\",\"root_revision\":\"1335fa854c41be9c6811e5791829faade73ece84e33e655b4e3e612cbfec641e\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Two Small Pl006 Gaps Left Open By 141\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**1. Severity is not re-tunable.** PL006 is absent from `_KNOWN_POLICY_RULES`, so a user cannot adjust its severity via `.skilllint.json` the way they can for other policy rules. This matters more than usual given #145 \u2014 the live CLI returns a *warning* where PL006 emits an *error*, and a user who agrees with the CLI has no supported way to say so.\\n\\n**2. Authority metadata points at the wrong origin.** `check_pl006` is registered with `authority={\\\"origin\\\": \\\"github.com/jamie-bitflight/claude_skills\\\"}`, but its message and suggestion both cite an actual Claude Code schema URL. Compare `fm_series.py`, which uses `{\\\"origin\\\": \\\"anthropic.com\\\", ...}`.\\n\\nThe consequence is not cosmetic: `skilllint docs fetch-authorities` walks normalized authority URLs, so PL006's real source is never fetched into the vendor cache, and the rule cannot be offline-verified against the document it actually cites.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why These Were Not Fixed In 141\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#141's ordering was load-bearing \u2014 delete the relocation auto-fix, then widen the allowlist \u2014 and both of these are unrelated metadata concerns that would have widened that diff for no benefit.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #141 \u2014 the fix that surfaced both\\n- #145 \u2014 the severity evidence conflict that makes gap 1 matter\\n- #40 \u2014 23 rules carrying `authority = None`; same provenance surface\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b8aaadee1b306054037ec6250fa671363115491ca830204c31f9c7290e19f105\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-P3g\"}"}